  <h2>The MondayMotivator</h2>
  <p>I started the MondayMotivator in 2004 as a way to stay in contact with prospects and clients, prove you could send weekly emails and start the week on a positive note. I didn't miss a Monday for over 10 years. Put it on hiatus because I overthought my business, and then I haven't missed a Monday since.</p>
  <p><a href="/mondaymotivator/">Read the archive →</a></p>
  <p><a href="https://spike.co.nz/sign-me-up" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get the MondayMotivator by email →</a></p>

  <h2>The Four Factors</h2>
  <p>Belief, Programming the Mind, Mental Posture and Focus are four practical lenses I use to make sense of thoughts, responses and behaviour. They now provide the main themes for exploring the MondayMotivator archive.</p>
  <p><a href="/four-factors/">Understand the Four Factors →</a></p>

  <h2>Light Your Own Fire</h2>
  <p>The book I co-wrote with best-selling author and Psychology Coach Charles Donoghue. We spent 12 months putting this together from the best of both of our writing. Alison Rowe — winner of both the Boston Marathon and New York City Marathon in the same year — wrote the endorsement.</p>
